difform:
a. Irregular in form; -- opposed to uniform; anomalous;
   hence, unlike; dissimilar; as, to difform corolla, the parts of which
   do not correspond in size or proportion; difform leaves.

goldylocks:
n. A plant of several species of the genus Chrysocoma; --
   so called from the tufts of yellow flowers which terminate the stems;
   also, the Ranunculus auricomus, a kind of buttercup.
